  "reason": "Evidence: config_038 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat) achieved the best accuracy so far (0.6186), a large jump over the singleprofile baseline (0.5266). The multiprofile + avgpool + concat + resnet50 pipeline is validated as strong. The weakest component in that pipeline is the RNA encoder: pca_n2000 is a linear dimensionality reduction that may discard nonlinear biological signal. Question: Does upgrading the RNA encoder to scgpt (a pretrained transformer capturing gene-expression semantics) while holding all other components fixed improve validation accuracy beyond 0.6186? This is the single most impactful untested change on the current best configuration. Why this is the best use of experiment 4: it directly exploits the strongest evidence (config_038) with a one-variable extension, reducing uncertainty about whether a richer RNA representation can push accuracy higher. Expected relative cost: scgpt is a transformer-based encoder applied per-cell across multiple profiles, so this will be moderately more expensive than config_038's 36.42 GPU-hr run—estimated ~45–55 GPU hours—making it the most expensive option among the single-change extensions, but justified because it targets the component most likely to yield a meaningful accuracy gain."
}

